# 7. Common Themes

Several common themes were identified across the ten papers.

## Theme 1: AI improves diagnosis and prediction

AI and machine learning can analyse large amounts of medical information and identify patterns that can support early diagnosis and prediction.

Examples include:

- Chronic kidney disease
- Sepsis
- Breast cancer
- Medical imaging
- Chronic disease monitoring

## Theme 2: AI supports healthcare professionals

The literature generally presents AI as a tool that can assist healthcare professionals rather than completely replace them.

AI can provide:

- Risk predictions
- Clinical alerts
- Diagnostic assistance
- Patient monitoring
- Data analysis

## Theme 3: Explainability and trust

Several papers emphasise that healthcare AI must be understandable and transparent.

Explainable AI can help clinicians understand why an AI system produced a particular prediction.

## Theme 4: Privacy and security

Healthcare data is highly sensitive. Therefore, AI systems need strong privacy and security protections.

Federated learning is one approach that can allow models to learn from distributed data without requiring all patient data to be centrally collected.

## Theme 5: Fairness and bias

AI systems can reproduce biases contained in their training data.

Therefore, healthcare AI needs to be evaluated across different patient populations to ensure that it does not disadvantage particular groups.

## Theme 6: Governance and accountability

As AI becomes more advanced, questions arise regarding who is responsible when an AI system makes an incorrect recommendation.

Governance, regulation and accountability are therefore becoming increasingly important.

